nt": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ArPtLHVntS74ARHsJZp7Mr", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57733, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ArPtLHVntS74ARHsJZp7Mr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63042, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't send it again. That avoided a duplicate incident and a second page to on-call.\n- The incident describes what happened, the rollback and the orchestrator error. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and of the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback. v2.3.1's release candidate had also failed health checks in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AB19gZFg5mbL4R8hfJZ7bL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y5tfppQu6qtXGTRZ6kPrdG", "caller": {"type": 