ing the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and the orchestrator partial-rollout error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ArPtLHVntS74ARHsJZp7Mr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't send it again. That avoided a duplicate incident and a second page to on-call.\n- The incident describes what happened, the rollback and the orchestrator error. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and of the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback. v2.3.1's release candidate had also failed health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}